          "_baseline_note_raises": "AUTHORISED RE-RECORD of `raises` on THIS handler only (`backend_app.routers.support.create_ticket`, POST /api/support/tickets) — ONE ADDED entry, `503 / str`, and nothing removed or retyped. Authorised by the committed guard that requires it: `tests/test_exception_swallow_regression.py::TestCreateTicketExceptionSwallow::test_db_error_returns_503_not_a_fabricated_ticket_id`. SUP-02: the insert named four columns `support_tickets` did not declare (related_feature, strategy_id, order_id, attachment), so PostgREST rejected every statement with PGRST204; the handler caught it, logged a WARNING, parked the ticket in a process-local `_in_memory_tickets` dict and returned 200 with a real ticket id. Users were told reports were filed that nothing stored, from 2026-08-29 until migration 072. The 503 is a genuine contract change and is recorded as one: a caller must now treat 503 as 'not filed, safe to retry'."
        }
      ],
      "method": "POST",
