          "_baseline_note_raises": "AUTHORISED RE-RECORD of `raises` on THIS handler only (`backend_app.routers.support.add_comment`, POST /api/support/tickets/{ticket_id}/comments) — ONE ADDED entry, `503 / str`, beside the existing 400 and 404, and nothing removed or retyped. Authorised by the committed guard that requires it: `tests/test_exception_swallow_regression.py::TestAddCommentExceptionSwallow::test_db_error_returns_503_rather_than_reporting_the_reply_sent`. Same SUP-02 cause as api_calls[3]: `ticket_comments` had no `attachment` column, so a reply carrying attachment metadata was rejected while the caller received 200. Both comment writes were also fire-and-forget (`.execute()` unawaited), so against an async client the statement never reached the database at all — the bug class commit 475cf655 went through this codebase for."
